course: dictionary
lesson: 1413
title: Carefully: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Carefully» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and it comes from the adjective «careful» with -ly added. «She walks carefully on the icy playground» tells you how she walks.
explain: The word has two meanings. First, it means with care, slowly and paying attention so you make no mistakes, as in «count the turns carefully». Second, it means gently, so you do not break or hurt something, as in «swept up carefully with a brush».
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap a meaning into the sentence. Try «with care» and then «gently». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning the writer wanted.
fact: «Carefully» is an adverb, made from the adjective «careful» by adding -ly.
fact: «Carefully» means with care, slowly and paying attention so you do not make mistakes.
fact: «Carefully» can also mean gently, so you do not break or hurt something.
fact: In school, instructions often say «read carefully» or «check carefully».
fact: Broken glass is swept up carefully, never picked up with bare hands, because it can cut you.
exercise: «Broken glass is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan.» What does carefully mean here? | *Gently and safely, so nobody gets hurt | Without using a brush | Very fast and noisy | Only once a week
exercise: Your teacher writes «check carefully». What does she want you to do? | Ask someone else to do it for you | Check it very quickly without looking | Skip the check altogether | *Look again with attention, so you make no mistakes
exercise: Find the adverb in this sentence: «She walks carefully on the icy playground.» | icy | She | *carefully | playground
test:  The nests are collected carefully from cave walls. Why? | Because the nests are cheap | *So the birds can still breed | To make the cave walls dirty | To stop people eating bird's nest soup
test: «Careful» is the adjective. Which word is the adverb form that matches it? | carefree | *carefully | caring | careless
exam: «Being tricked once does not mean trusting no-one; it means trusting carefully, knowing the signs.» What does trusting carefully mean? | Trusting only on Sundays | Never trusting anyone at all | Trusting everyone at once without a thought | *Trusting with care, watching for the signs
